<span class="boltz-interface-note">
  <span class="note-copy">The difference is easiest to see in the raw tool outputs. V1 surfaced the scalar score directly but returned only a directory containing the predicted structures:</span>
  <span class="output-block" aria-label="Original Boltz tool output">
    <span><b>binding_probability:</b> 0.1583</span>
    <span><b>affinity_pred_value:</b> 0.7236</span>
    <span><b>cif_dir:</b> boltz_results/call_1/...</span>
  </span>
  <span class="note-copy">The agent then had to locate the individual CIF files itself before inspecting the poses.</span>
  <span class="note-copy v2-copy">V2 instead attached the result to a registered candidate and returned the pose files explicitly:</span>
  <span class="output-block" aria-label="Redesigned Boltz tool output">
    <span><b>candidate_id:</b> C001</span>
    <span><b>binding_probability:</b> 0.1665</span>
    <span><b>pose_files:</b></span>
    <span class="indent">model_0.cif</span>
    <span class="indent">model_1.cif</span>
    <span class="indent muted">...</span>
    <span class="indent">model_9.cif</span>
  </span>
</span>

